// Found via effect_row_open.vibe-adjacent investigation (2026-07-23): an
// inline `EFn` lambda literal -- one written directly at a call site, never
// let-bound to a name -- performing an effect, used to produce genuinely
// INVALID wasm ("invalid signature index" at compile time) or crash at
// runtime ("null function or function signature mismatch"), in two related
// shapes that both evaded every existing local-closure fix (#786/#1069/
// #1070), because all of them pattern-match specifically on
// `ELet(name, EFn(...), body)` -- an inline literal with no enclosing let
// has no name for any of that machinery to latch onto:
//
//   1. A bare IIFE: `(() -> Int with Log { perform ...; 42 })()`.
//   2. An inline literal passed as a CALL ARGUMENT (not the callee) to an
//      ordinary named function whose body genuinely calls its parameter
//      internally (not a #1070 trivial same-arity forward) -- e.g.
//      `with_log(() -> Int with Log { perform ...; 42 })` where
//      `with_log = (f) -> { handle { f() } with Log { ... } }`.
//
// Fixed in desugar_trait_dict.vibe's dlh_hoist_expr: an IIFE is desugared
// into the already-handled `ELet(fresh, EFn(...), fresh())` shape; a
// literal-EFn call ARGUMENT is let-bound immediately before the call
// (`dlh_letbind_literal_args`, semantics-preserving left-to-right
// evaluation order). Both reduce to the existing, separately-verified
// ELet/EFn hoist logic -- no new closure-conversion code was needed. Note
// this is NOT the row-polymorphism gap (docs/effect-evidence-passing.md
// 追記23) -- the effect row here is fully monomorphic (`{ Log }` on both
// sides), and the crash reproduces with zero row-variable involvement at
// all; it just happened to be found while investigating that fixture.
//
// Scope: this fix only covers a CAPTURE-FREE literal (confirmed via direct
// testing -- reduces to a plain top-level hoist, exactly like a named
// function). A CAPTURING literal passed the same way (as a HOF argument,
// not called directly at its own definition site) still falls through to
// #1070's already-known, already-deferred general case: the synthesized
// let-binding this fix introduces makes `dlh_marker_only_called_directly`
// correctly see the closure used as a VALUE (passed into `with_log`, not
// called directly in the visible scope), so #1069's closure-conversion
// safely declines rather than risk an unsound rewrite. This fixture
// deliberately stays capture-free to pin only what's actually fixed.
//
//   IIFE (handled by an OUTER handle, not a nested one): perform resolves
//   to 5 -> 5
//   with_log(inline lambda, no captures): perform resolves to 5 -> 5
//   total: 5 + 5 = 10
effect Log {
  Get -> Int
}

let with_log = (f: () -> Int with Log) -> Int {
  handle { f() } with Log {
    Get => resume(5)
  }
}

export let main = () -> Int {
  let iife_result = handle {
    (() -> Int with Log {
      perform Log::Get
    })()
  } with Log {
    Get => resume(5)
  }
  let hof_result = with_log(() -> Int with Log {
    perform Log::Get
  })
  iife_result + hof_result
}

test "main produces its recorded value" {
  // #1571: expectation moved off a `__DATA__` tail; `vibe test --update`
  // rewrites this literal.
  inspect(main(), "10")
}
